menu "SA11x0"

config SND_SA11X0_SOC
	tristate "SoC Audio for the Intel/StrongARM SA-1100/SA-1110 chip"
	depends on ARCH_SA1100 || COMPILE_TEST
	help
	  Say Y or M if you want to add support for codecs attached to the
	  SA-1100/SA-1110 SSP interface. You will also need to select the
	  audio interfaces to support below. The SA-1100 and SA-1110 are
	  the StrongARM based SoCs found, for example, in the HP iPAQ h3800
	  family of handheld computers.

config SND_SA11X0_SOC_SSP
	tristate "SoC Audio via SA-1110 SSP ports"
	depends on SND_SA11X0_SOC
	select SND_SOC_GENERIC_DMAENGINE_PCM
	help
	  Say Y or M here to build the CPU DAI driver for the Ser4 SSP port of
	  the SA-1110. It transfers audio samples to the codec by DMA, in the
	  16-bit TI synchronous serial frame format. The SSP drives the bit
	  clock and the frame, dividing the bit clock from a reference clock
	  on GPIO19. Only playback is supported.

endmenu
